            "review_text": "MAJ\n5 contributions\n0\nDisappointing Experience – Overpriced Tourist Trap\nFeb 2026 • Solo\nI usually try to follow local recommendations when dining out, and this place looked full of locals, so I thought it would be authentic. Unfortunately, I should have read the reviews first.\n\nI strongly suspect there’s some sort of scam targeting tourists here. I paid $62 for a very small meal, so small, in fact, that I had to eat elsewhere afterward. Checking other seafood spots on the same street, their prices were higher, but based on local living costs, I doubt locals are paying anywhere near what tourists are charged here.\n\nThe food wasn’t fresh or particularly tasty, and the staff were rude, just as others have mentioned. It’s not even a beachfront restaurant, so the high prices can’t be justified by location.\n\nIf you’re visiting the area, I would strongly recommend skipping this one. It’s overpriced and seems designed to take advantage of tourists.\nRead more\nWritten March 14, 2026",
